        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 57-year-old female admitted on 29/09/2022 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, pulse oximetry, arterial blood gas analysis, chest X-ray, and blood tests were performed to confirm the exacerbation and exclude complications such as pneumonia or pulmonary embolism. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of severe airflow obstruction. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged on 30/09/2022 with an optimised inhaler regimen. Please ensure follow-up including pulmonary rehabilitation referral and smoking cessation support. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
